WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:07.839
David, do you think it's a problem that people
are making huge amounts of money from the

00:00:07.839 --> 00:00:11.330
development and manufacture of coronavirus
vaccines?

00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:16.390
Listen, I think that my view on this will
probably anger most people other than like

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:20.310
Social Democrats that are exactly in my political
space.

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:22.360
I think there has to be a middle ground on
this.

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:24.220
Now, on
the one hand,

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:31.320
we, as Bernie Sanders recently said, we can't
allow these pharmaceutical companies to hold

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:37.280
governments and and humans hostage when it
comes to something like health.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:44.200
As I've said before, demand for health care
services and medications and vaccines is inelastic.

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:51.370
What I mean by that is my appendectomy right
up until the day at which my appendix swelled

00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:52.870
and became painful.

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:55.620
I don't care what the price is for appendectomies.

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:56.620
I don't want one.

00:00:56.620 --> 00:00:57.620
I don't need one.

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:02.300
And then all of a sudden when I require an
emergency appendectomy,

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:03.739
they
have me over a barrel.

00:01:03.739 --> 00:01:10.649
I need and and I must find a way to pay any
price for an appendectomy because health care

00:01:10.649 --> 00:01:14.560
services and demand is is completely inelastic.

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:18.030
So we need health is what we would call a
special.

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:25.630
It can't just be left to the free market now,
on the other hand, as I've said before, as

00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:27.889
a social Democrat,
I don't

00:01:27.889 --> 00:01:33.719
need I'm fine with the market dictating what
video game consoles get made and who makes

00:01:33.719 --> 00:01:34.899
them and what they charge.

00:01:34.899 --> 00:01:35.899
I'm OK with that.

00:01:35.899 --> 00:01:37.100
I'm fine with that.

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:38.210
Mobile phones.

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:39.210
I'm OK.

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:42.990
You know, I don't need the government involved
in regulating mobile phone prices.

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:45.869
I think that the market and that is a consumer
product.

00:01:45.869 --> 00:01:50.749
It's I'm fine with that, assuming that everybody's
playing within a regulatory framework and

00:01:50.749 --> 00:01:58.610
to some degree, the the smartest, best people
we have are going to be more likely to line

00:01:58.610 --> 00:02:04.130
up to do things like developing a vaccine
for the virus quickly if there is something

00:02:04.130 --> 00:02:05.569
there for them.

00:02:05.569 --> 00:02:09.940
Now, many people will point to Russia and
say, well, look at Russia.

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:15.560
Russia developed the Sputnik vaccine basically
as quickly as the Moderna and Pfizer vaccines

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:17.090
were developed.

00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:20.209
And because they did, they didn't even finish
testing it.

00:02:20.209 --> 00:02:22.910
They they started using it even more quickly.

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:29.409
If you understand the authoritarian nature
of Russia, you would realize that although

00:02:29.409 --> 00:02:34.579
it did happen essentially as quickly as Pfizer
and Moderna, which which we will talk about,

00:02:34.579 --> 00:02:39.760
it wasn't just because out of the the goodwill
and desire it took place.

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:44.379
You're talking about an authoritarian situation
there, as we've been talking about for decades

00:02:44.379 --> 00:02:45.379
at this point in time.

00:02:45.379 --> 00:02:49.390
So, I mean, listen, the Turkish couple in
Germany that developed

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:54.250
what is now called the Pfizer vaccine, they
are now very wealthy.

00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:58.250
They invested time and money in developing
that vaccine.

00:02:58.250 --> 00:03:00.870
And now there is a payoff.

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:04.950
If there was absolutely no payoff, then would
they do it again?

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:06.269
I mean, maybe not.

00:03:06.269 --> 00:03:12.250
And you look at Pfizer, Pfizer increased revenue
two percent after investing billions of dollars

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:16.510
in R&amp;D and production on this vaccine.

00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:17.510
Is that bad?

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:18.510
I mean, two percent?

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:19.510
Yeah, it's a huge company.

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:20.830
It's a huge amount of money.

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:26.680
You could apply the same logic to researchers
of other vaccines.

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:32.129
Don't we want people entering the field of
science and developing things that can be

00:03:32.129 --> 00:03:33.519
lifesaving?

00:03:33.519 --> 00:03:36.120
Of course, we need to ensure access.

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:38.560
Of course, we need situations where things
are subsidized.

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:45.020
Of course, Bernie is right when he says, you
know, the patenting of these vaccines, when

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:50.200
it comes to them being produced in other countries,
we need to take control of this.

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:55.250
We can't do it in a way where other countries
are prevented from making the vaccine.

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:56.879
Of course, we need to do all of those things.

00:03:56.879 --> 00:04:01.569
But at the same time, we want to incentivize
people to get into these fields.

00:04:01.569 --> 00:04:06.349
If the belief is the way you make a lot of
money is by, you know, I don't know, becoming

00:04:06.349 --> 00:04:12.040
a celebrity or an athlete or a,
you know,

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:16.389
high priced lawyer or a consultant or whatever,
and then people don't get into these fields

00:04:16.389 --> 00:04:18.600
of medical research that we're all worse off.

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:22.080
So I believe there has to be a middle ground.

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:26.150
Maybe the government needs to be involved
in determining what are fair prices.

00:04:26.150 --> 00:04:32.250
You know, all of these things have caveats,
but context is crucial.

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:38.370
And when you say should it be possible for
pharmaceutical companies to hold the world

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:42.360
hostage, charging three hundred dollars per
vaccine dose?

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:44.960
No, no, that shouldn't be possible.

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:50.030
Should it be OK for people that are developing
lifesaving technologies to be rewarded in

00:04:50.030 --> 00:04:52.520
a way that's commensurate with what they are
doing?

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:54.470
Yeah, to some degree that should be OK.

00:04:54.470 --> 00:04:55.470
And you know what?

00:04:55.470 --> 00:04:57.110
If they make a ton of money, they should pay
a lot of taxes.

00:04:57.110 --> 00:05:01.820
And all of the other economic policy that
we and Bernie and others have been talking

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:06.710
about, I think context is key and there has
to be a middle path here.

00:05:06.710 --> 00:05:12.780
And I'm curious to hear from you where you
fall on this issue, make sure you are a member

00:05:12.780 --> 00:05:36.990
at join Pakman Dotcom to 
get access to 

00:05:36.990 --> 00:05:41.780
the bonus show.

00:05:41.780 --> 00:06:19.880
Otherwise, I'll see you on Monday.

